WEBVTT

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:09.730
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:20.090
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.480
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:06.920
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:14.220
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:20.850
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:28.290
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:38.320
I am Wauf, the captain of the Messis.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:44.890
The highland aerial base, found on
a Chor Tempest scouting flight…

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:47.330
…has since vanished without a trace.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:51.500
Four of Chor Tempest’s Simouns
have already left the ship.

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:57.010
The sharp surge in enemy attacks
the last 12 hours is worrisome.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:02.510
The Messis has been left with
only two Simouns on board.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.210
I’m getting a bad feeling…

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:06.520
Captain!

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.770
Everyone’s in position.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:11.440
The kitchen staff
can be relieved for now.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.930
Yes, sir!

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:34.710
<b>The Emerald Ri Majon</b>

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:49.810
I’m going to do it for you.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.310
The Emerald Ri Majon.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.820
He sure does have
a screwed-up face.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.570
You think he takes after his owner?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.200
Roatreamon?

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.660
Or maybe the one who made him.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:11.810
How can you laugh?

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:13.710
We’re in trouble!

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.150
A-Aircraft sighted!

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:23.090
Um… Um…

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.030
Nine o’clock! A fleet of planes!

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.680
Non-Simoun!

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.030
Nine o’clock!
A fleet of planes! Non-Simoun!

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:32.460
We should assume
they’ve spotted us.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.860
Six o’clock! A fleet of planes!

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:35.900
Take us down lower!

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.900
Any lower and we’ll hit trees.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:42.780
It doesn’t matter! Mow them down!
Find a hiding place for this ship!

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:51.110
There’s a hill at one o’clock.

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:54.250
Turn us around at full speed!
Prepare to land!

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:01.510
We can fight with two Simouns,
but it’s over if the Messis falls!

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:05.720
Baby birds who’ve lost their mother
are doomed to starve to death.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:08.970
Don’t say things like that.
You’ll frighten the child.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:11.480
I’m not…

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:13.850
Rimone’s not scared at all, see?

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.450
Come on. Let’s go too.

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:32.660
Sibylla Dominüra…

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:41.380
The Simouns are the vehicles
of the gods… They can’t fall.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.180
What should we do, Dominüra?
Pursue the enemy?

00:04:59.180 --> 00:04:59.820
No.

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:03.820
The priority now is
to protect the Messis.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:07.120
We’ll flank and keep
its launch position undetected.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.990
Good idea. We’ll attack by land,
using it as a smokescreen.

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:12.040
Roger.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:15.000
You know what, Aer?

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.190
Rimone?

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:20.060
I kind of brought Roatreamon’s
stuffed animal with me.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:54.200
Drop anchor!

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:55.330
Now dropping anchor!

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:57.530
Captain, I believe we’re
going to get away with this.

00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:59.350
Looks like it.

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:03.560
So we pulled the wool
over their eyes after all, eh?

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:09.530
It seems they’re gone. Aer…

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:10.570
Not yet.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:20.620
They made it look like they’d gone,
but they were keeping an eye out.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.250
Should we head back now?

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:26.780
Hey…

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:31.630
I have no idea how to survive here.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:36.890
Having honed our war skills
isn’t anything to brag about.

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.260
War skills, did you say?

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:43.530
That’s right. It’s my war skills…

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:49.810
Techniques for survival…
I’ve got to learn more about them.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:04.170
It’s quiet here, isn’t it?

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.600
Dominüra?

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:14.700
You said you’d do it for me, right?

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:17.470
The Emerald Ri Majon…

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:24.330
I never intended to put
such a burden on you.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:29.060
It’s just that unless I know
I’m doing it for someone…

00:08:29.060 --> 00:08:33.570
…the way I am right now,
I have no chance of moving forward.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:47.750
I don’t understand…

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:52.510
I do understand
how you feel, Dominüra.

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:57.970
But I don’t understand
why I understand.

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:05.380
Because you’re my pair… That’s why.

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:17.280
We should’ve realized it sooner.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:20.810
So you’re saying
the others were lured away?

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:24.040
Yes.
They’ve splintered Chor Tempest…

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:26.790
…forcing it
to disperse its combat power.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:30.920
It’s going to be all right, Rimone.

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:35.220
They still haven’t
pinpointed our exact location.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.800
Sibylla Dominüra…

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.760
I’m sure you’re
as aware of this as I am.

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:42.510
The sun will rise soon.

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:47.510
Once the enemy attacks again,
there’ll be no escaping detection.

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:51.770
In that case, what kind
of choices do we have?

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:55.170
One would be to wait for
the four Simouns’ return…

00:09:55.170 --> 00:10:00.050
…and sit tight until we can launch
a counterattack against the enemy.

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:01.710
The other would be…

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:05.510
…to make our escape from
this airspace as soon as possible.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:10.130
Then what will become
of Neviril and the others?

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:11.170
Well…

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.860
This is your opinion, is it not?

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:19.340
As things stand, the survival rate for
the Simouns that have yet to return…

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:22.800
…is extremely low.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:25.470
How can you utter
such groundless rubbish?

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:29.280
Chor Tempest is Kyuukoku’s
finest chor! We can’t fall!

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:30.600
You’re absolutely right.

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:34.610
They’re all coming back for sure.
So try to calm down.

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:38.820
Paraietta!

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:41.620
I’ll search for the Simouns.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:43.450
What about the Messis?

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:47.730
The captain’s view about Shoukoku’s
new aircraft attacking again…

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:49.210
…isn’t guaranteed!

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.210
Your behavior is quite violent.

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:53.090
Rimone.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:56.500
I want you to come with me.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:57.700
You and I…

00:10:57.700 --> 00:10:59.590
Rimone is my pair.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:01.340
Dominüra!

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:04.660
And I am Rimone’s pair.

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:14.230
Why are you doing this?

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:21.210
What’s going on with you? All of you!

00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:23.950
How can you stay so calm?

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.520
When your own
comrades are in peril?

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:32.510
I could never bring myself
to abandon my comrades!

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:36.090
You don’t mean comrades.
You mean Neviril, don’t you?

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.580
Since when is Neviril your underling?

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:41.230
My underling?

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:44.910
Sibylla Aurea is
Chor Tempest’s highest sibylla.

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:47.470
Thinking someone
like you can protect her…

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:49.850
…is gross arrogance.

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:56.210
Fine.

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.150
I’ll go with you.

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:09.080
Rimone, you and I will go with them.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:13.000
But give me a little time
before we leave. I won’t be long.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:17.880
Besides, in the state
you’re in right now…

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:21.810
…you can’t activate the Simoun
with Aer, can you, Paraietta?

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:47.490
Sibylla Dominüra!

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:50.620
I see someone else got here first.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:57.750
Without something to believe in…

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:01.000
…none of us can even
plant our feet on the earth.

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:05.760
In my case, that was Kyuukoku,
as well as Tempus Spatium.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:14.020
What are you…

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:20.820
The Simouns taught me something…

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:24.280
Something I never wanted to know.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.280
Please tell me…
What was it that you…

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:30.330
What on earth did you…

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:34.750
Forget about that day, Waporif.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:35.790
But…

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:39.790
That’s the last warning
I’ll be giving you.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:51.470
As we thought.

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:53.220
What is it?

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:55.850
Planes sighted at eight o’clock!

00:13:55.850 --> 00:14:00.730
They got here sooner than I thought.
We probably don’t have time to run.

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:04.990
The Messis will remain moored
here and attempt a counterattack!

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:08.950
Let’s go, Aer.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.830
You all right?

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:12.950
I want you, Aer.

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:17.460
Because unless you come
with me, I can’t save Neviril.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:23.380
Sibylla Dominüra…

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:26.130
Please be safe.

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:27.770
You too.

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:31.240
Rimone?

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.100
I forgot to give it back!

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:52.180
Do you see that?

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:54.040
They’re flying so high!

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.300
They’re practically Simouns!

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:13.090
Dominüra! Rimone!

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:17.100
Aer, let’s go! The Falcon Ri Majon!

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:29.110
Aer! The Falcon
Ri Majon one more time.

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:32.320
Right! As many times as it takes!

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:41.710
Rimone, which Ri Majon can we do
that has the most destructive power?

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:43.960
The Wave Crest Ri Majon!

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:07.320
Rimone! One more time!

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:09.320
Wave Crest Ri Majon!

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:14.320
But why?

00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:17.890
How?

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:20.950
They’ve made huge technological
advances in such a short time.

00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:25.960
They haven’t reached the Simouns’
level yet, but such great numbers…

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:28.170
The Fish Silhouette Ri Majon!

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:35.180
It’s no good! We can’t do
Ri Majons with all this interference!

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:40.100
The Messis!

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:47.310
The Emerald Ri Majon…

00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:51.620
Has the time come for us to do it?

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:55.780
But I don’t know…

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:56.820
Afraid?

00:16:56.820 --> 00:17:00.540
No, not me. But…

00:17:01.190 --> 00:17:03.490
You’re afraid, aren’t you, Dominüra?

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:08.790
Who ever thought you’d
understand me to that degree?

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:12.080
What I saw that day…

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:14.300
It was a terrifying sight.

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:21.140
It destroyed every last shred of my
pride and shattered all I believed in.

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:25.410
But that’s not what I’m afraid of.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:30.430
Beyond that terrible sight,
I caught a glimpse of something.

00:17:30.430 --> 00:17:32.370
That’s what I’m afraid of.

00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:33.900
What was it?

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:38.870
I can’t describe it in words.
But if I had to give it a name…

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:41.620
I’d call it hope.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:45.210
For the Messis…

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:47.870
They’re fighting so
that we might be saved.

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:50.840
They’re fighting for us!

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:53.040
Captain!

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:57.760
Don’t let the sibyllae’s
prayers be in vain!

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:02.350
We’ll draw the enemy’s attention
so the priestesses can escape!

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:04.210
Yes, sir!

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:12.650
What the?

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:14.650
Madness! Are they trying to die?

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:16.980
Are they doing it for us?

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:19.160
Yes, I’m sure they are.

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:26.870
Prepare the cannons!

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:31.130
Dominüra…

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:32.320
Yes.

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:34.820
I want to!

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:36.210
No matter what may lie ahead?

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:39.750
The Emerald Ri Majon.

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:47.410
I guess we lost sight of them, huh?

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:48.730
I suppose.

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:54.400
What is this? This feeling?

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:57.780
It feels so familiar
yet so relentlessly cold.

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:58.820
Neviril!

00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:01.820
Over there… Look.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:05.290
That’s…

00:19:06.050 --> 00:19:08.040
The Emerald Ri Majon!

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:20.840
What’s going on?

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:23.600
Stop it, Dominüra! Rimone!

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:26.120
You’ve got to stop!

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:27.810
That’s the Emerald…

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:32.480
But why?

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:36.190
Hold up, who’s doing
the Emerald Ri Majon?

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:40.550
I never thought
we’d ever see it again…

00:19:41.190 --> 00:19:42.450
We’re heading right back!

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:44.730
You’re sure? That’s…

00:19:44.730 --> 00:19:46.450
No! They’ll be killed!

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:50.160
Stop it… please…

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:54.790
Stop it!

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:03.600
Rimone…

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:05.300
Dominüra?

00:20:06.610 --> 00:20:07.970
I’m not afraid.

00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:11.240
Right, I’m not afraid either.

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:15.630
We’re together.

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:17.020
Together…

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:20.320
Forever and ever.

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:23.320
Yes, forever and ever.

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:57.520
Nothing’s changed.

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:03.540
Wait. Where did
Dominüra and Rimone go?

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:04.970
They’re gone.

00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:10.610
They don’t give up.

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:20.920
Neviril…

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:22.930
Captain! It’s the Simouns!

00:21:22.930 --> 00:21:25.260
Thank goodness! They’re all safe!

00:21:27.990 --> 00:21:30.190
Sibylla Dominüra…

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:35.010
What’s this?

00:21:35.010 --> 00:21:36.070
What’s going on?

00:21:36.070 --> 00:21:37.480
Hey!

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:38.770
C-Captain!

00:21:39.470 --> 00:21:42.820
Directly overhead…
I-It’s the Arcus Prima!

00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:54.700
That was a close shave,
but it seems we’re in time.

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:58.460
Sorry to have kept
you waiting, my sibyllae.

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:01.710
Everybody…

00:22:07.530 --> 00:22:10.680
I am Wauf, the captain of the Messis.

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:13.770
In the end, we survived.

00:22:14.570 --> 00:22:19.730
Thanks to the Arcus Prima and the
return of Chor Tempest’s Simouns.

00:22:22.010 --> 00:22:27.530
But as for the Simoun flown by Sibylla
Dominüra and Sibylla Rimone…

00:22:28.220 --> 00:22:31.710
We never found
even the slightest trace.

00:22:41.100 --> 00:22:47.810
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.810 --> 00:22:52.050
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.050 --> 00:22:59.090
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.090 --> 00:23:06.750
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:19.610
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.610 --> 00:23:24.780
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.780 --> 00:23:28.790
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.790 --> 00:23:32.640
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:38.150
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.690 --> 00:23:44.210
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.210 --> 00:23:47.610
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:53.310
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.310 --> 00:23:59.470
